354873.statement:
Let $N=m_1s_1+\cdots+m_Ls_L$ with $0<s_1<\cdots<s_L$ and $m_i>0$, set $N_i=m_is_i$, and let $f_i$ be principal nilpotent elements of ${\mathfrak {gl}}_{N_i}$. Let

$$
{\mathcal W}_L^k\left({\mathfrak {gl}}_N,({\mathfrak {gl}}_{N_1},\dots,{
}{\mathfrak {gl}}_{N_L}),(f_1,\dots,f_L)\right)
$$

be the associated iterated W-algebra, and let $\beta\gamma^d$ denote the vertex algebra of a pair of symplectic bosons with multiplicity $d$. **Iterated W-algebra isomorphism conjecture.** There is an isomorphism of vertex algebras

$$
{\mathcal W}_L^k\left({\mathfrak {gl}}_N,({\mathfrak {gl}}_{N_1},\dots,{
}{\mathfrak {gl}}_{N_L}),(f_1,\dots,f_L)\right)\cong {\mathcal W}^k({\mathfrak {gl}}_N,f)\otimes\bigotimes_{1\leq i<j\leq L}\beta\gamma^{m_im_j(s_j-s_i)}.
$$

The character identity preceding this claim is proved in the cited proposition, but the corresponding vertex-algebra isomorphism is presented as a conjecture.
